{"code_citation":"Tex. Prop. Code § 209.0051","title":"Open board meetings","category":"meetings","body":"A regular or special board meeting must be open to property owners, subject to the right of the board to adjourn a meeting and reconvene in closed executive session. Notice of a regular or special board meeting must be: (1) mailed, e-mailed, or hand-delivered to each property owner not later than the 10th day or earlier than the 60th day before the date of the meeting; or (2) provided at least 72 hours before the meeting in a manner described by the association's dedicatory instruments. SAMPLE EXCERPT — replace with full statutory text from statutes.capitol.texas.gov before production use.","source_url":"https://statutes.capitol.texas.gov/Docs/PR/htm/PR.209.htm#209.0051","effective_date":null}
{"code_citation":"Tex. Prop. Code § 209.0061","title":"Procedures for collection of fines","category":"fines","body":"A property owners' association may not enforce a restrictive covenant by levying a fine or other penalty unless the association has provided the owner with written notice of the alleged violation and an opportunity to cure or attend a hearing before the board. The notice must specify the violation, the amount of the fine, and the date by which the owner must cure the violation or request a hearing. SAMPLE EXCERPT — replace with full statutory text before production use.","source_url":"https://statutes.capitol.texas.gov/Docs/PR/htm/PR.209.htm#209.0061","effective_date":null}
{"code_citation":"Tex. Prop. Code § 209.005","title":"Association documents; production","category":"records","body":"A property owners' association shall make the books and records of the association available to an owner for inspection and copying, subject to reasonable rules adopted by the association. The owner must submit a written request specifying the items to be inspected. The association shall respond within 10 business days. SAMPLE EXCERPT — replace with full statutory text before production use.","source_url":"https://statutes.capitol.texas.gov/Docs/PR/htm/PR.209.htm#209.005","effective_date":null}
{"code_citation":"Tex. Prop. Code § 209.009","title":"Foreclosure sale prohibited in certain circumstances","category":"foreclosure","body":"A property owners' association may not foreclose a property owners' association's assessment lien if the debt securing the lien consists solely of: (1) fines assessed by the association; or (2) attorney's fees incurred by the association solely associated with fines assessed by the association. SAMPLE EXCERPT — replace with full statutory text before production use.","source_url":"https://statutes.capitol.texas.gov/Docs/PR/htm/PR.209.htm#209.009","effective_date":null}
